<title>UK: TABLE-RMC yr pre-exceps profit drops 9.1 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-RMC yr pre-exceps profit drops 9.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		68.9		   vs 80.3</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 18.7		   vs 17.6</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 26.5		   vs 25.05</p>
<p> Pretax		     296.2		  vs 337.1</p>
<p> Turnover		   4,559.7		vs 4,548.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Above pretax profits include exceptional items. Excluding exceptionals, pretax profit was 295.3 million stg in 1996 versus 324.9 million stg.</p>
<p>The company said it changed its accounting policy to use average exchange rates. Under the previous policy, pretax, pre-exceptionals profit would have been 275.8 million stg versus 329.3 million stg.</p>
<p>Analysts had forecast pre-tax profits in a range of 248.8 and 275.0 million stg.</p>
<p>Full company name - RMC Group Plc.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
